      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThis PR adds a TP2 deterministic inference test to AMD CI on MI35x. Today the deterministic test runs only at TP1, so nothing in CI covers the deterministic all-reduce, and multi-GPU regressions in deterministic mode go unnoticed. It follows up the review of #43788, which asked for multi-GPU coverage.\n\nThe existing test is not enough when simply run at TP2. With its 10 trials it passes on MI350X even without #34543, the fix for all-reduce inputs larger than the custom all-reduce buffer. With 50 trials the prefix log-probability check fails without that fix and passes with it.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `test/registered/attention/test_deterministic_tp2.py`: Qwen3-8B, TP2, Triton attention, `--enable-deterministic-inference`. One check: `prefix` mode with `--return-logprob` and 50 trials.\n- Registered on `stage-c-test-large-8-gpu-amd-mi35x`. There is no 2-GPU MI35x suite. About 5 minutes on 2 GPUs.\n- No code change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMI350X, `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm724-mi35x-20261012`, AMD CI environment (`SGLANG_USE_AITER=1`, `SGLANG_IS_IN_CI_AMD=1`), with #43788 applied in every run:\n\n| | Result | Time |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| With #34543 | OK in 10 of 10 runs | 242-314 s |\n| Without #34543 | fails in 2 of 2 runs (server out of memory / log-probabilities differ) | 419-518 s |\n| Existing 10-trial test at TP2, without #34543 | passes (does not catch it) | 180 s |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nTest only; no runtime change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38434960134](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38434960134)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38434960097](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38434960097)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38434960116](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38434960116)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
